    <bpmn:process id="W_W3947" name="W3947. AI Monitoring, Drift Detection &amp; Performance in Production" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Model in production; monitoring cycle
Frequency: Continuous + periodic review
Volume: All production models monitored
Owner: AI Governance / Data Science / IT
Participants: AI Governance, Data Science (links to VS-30.2), IT/MLOps (links to VS-27), Model Risk (links to VS-21), business AI owners (fraud VS-125, forecast VS-127, personalization VS-126), Privacy (links to VS-91)
Source: workflow W3947 — AI Monitoring, Drift Detection &amp; Performance in Production</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3947_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3947_Lane1" name="AI Governance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3947_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3947_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3947_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3947_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3947_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3947_Start3" name="Model in production; monitoring cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3947_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3947_Task4" name="AI Governance/IT/Data-Science operate production monitoring…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance/IT/Data-Science operate production monitoring: performance/accuracy, data drift (input distribution shift), concept drift (input-output relationship change), prediction/confidence distribution, fairness drift (links to W3937), and operational health (latency, throughput — links to POS SLA profile §15.3)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Data Science / IT
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3947_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3947_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3947_Task5" name="AI Governance/Model-Risk define drift/performance thresholds and alerting…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance/Model-Risk define drift/performance thresholds and alerting, trigger investigation and retraining (links to W3948) or fallback (links to W3940) when breached, and document decisions
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Model Risk
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3947_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3947_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3947_Task6" name="AI Governance/business-owners review monitoring dashboards monthly…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AI Governance/business-owners review monitoring dashboards monthly (per-use-case: fraud loss-rate links to VS-125, forecast accuracy links to VS-127, personalization lift links to VS-126), and feed learnings to model owners
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Business Owners
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3947_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3947_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3947_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3947_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3947_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-616 (ensure controlled execution — AI Lifecycle Operations, Assurance &amp; Value Realization (PA-128.3).) | - operational: drift monitoring and thresholds; operational: tuned thresholds and severity
Owner: AI Governance / Data Science / IT</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3947_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3947_Annotation8" targetRef="W3947_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
