    <bpmn:process id="W_W3952" name="W3952. AI Ethics Review Board, Stakeholder Engagement &amp; Continuous Improvement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: High-risk use-case; ethics cycle
Frequency: Per high-risk use-case + quarterly
Volume: AI ethics review board + stakeholder engagement
Owner: AI Governance / CIO
Participants: AI Governance, AI Ethics Review Board (cross-functional incl. Legal links to VS-100, Privacy links to VS-91, HR links to VS-19, Risk links to VS-21, business reps), CIO, Strategy (links to VS-33), Corporate Affairs (links to VS-14.3/VS-104)
Source: workflow W3952 — AI Ethics Review Board, Stakeholder Engagement &amp; Continuous Improvement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3952_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3952_Lane1" name="AI Ethics Review Board">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3952_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3952_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3952_Lane2" name="AI Governance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3952_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3952_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3952_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3952_Start4" name="High-risk use-case; ethics cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3952_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3952_Task5" name="AI Governance/AI-Ethics-Review-Board review high-risk/sensitive AI use-cases…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance/AI-Ethics-Review-Board review high-risk/sensitive AI use-cases (rights-affecting, customer-harm potential, employee-adjacent, GenAI customer-facing) for ethical acceptability, and approve/condition/reject
Responsible (R): AI Ethics Review Board / AI Governance
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead / CIO
Duration: Per use-case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3952_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3952_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3952_Task6" name="AI Governance/Corp-Affairs engage stakeholders (customers, employees…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance/Corp-Affairs engage stakeholders (customers, employees, regulators, industry) on AI use and BuildRight&#x27;s responsible-AI commitments, and manage AI-related reputation/communication (links to VS-14.3)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Corp Affairs
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3952_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3952_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3952_Task7" name="AI Governance/CIO run continuous improvement of the responsible-AI program…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AI Governance/CIO run continuous improvement of the responsible-AI program (incorporating incidents links to W3943, audit findings links to W3949, regulatory change links to W3944, maturity links to W3936), and report to the executive and Audit Committee (links to VS-33/VS-36)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / CIO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3952_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3952_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3952_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3952_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
