      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5512_Start7" name="Automation-Opportunity intake cycle (the per-workflow automation inventory refresh) or a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5512_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5512_Task8" name="AAP runs the quarterly candidate-scoring cycle: the per-workflow Automation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AAP runs the quarterly candidate-scoring cycle: the per-workflow Automation Opportunity inventory plus VS-133 process-mining surfaced candidates are scored hours × frequency × error rate × feasibility and ranked into the intake backlog
Responsible (R): AAP Platform Lead / Evaluation-AI-QA
Accountable (A): AAP Platform Lead
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5512_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5512_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5512_Task9" name="Owning product team proposes the agent with its Business Process Owner and a…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Owning product team proposes the agent with its Business Process Owner and a BPO case (task, volume, guardrail sketch, baseline human cost)
Responsible (R): Owning team PM / BPO
Accountable (A): Owning team Product Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/candidate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5512_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5512_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5512_Task10" name="SIB routes the sourcing per the sourcing-model §3 gate — platform-native…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: SIB routes the sourcing per the sourcing-model §3 gate — platform-native in-suite automation = use EBS; custom agent on the SEP paved road = build (vendor agent products are not a sourcing exit; foundation-model APIs remain commodity procurement under tier-1 TPRM) — the same gate, one more domain
Responsible (R): SIB / AAP Platform Lead
Accountable (A): Head of EA
Duration: At monthly SIB</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5512_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5512_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5512_Task11" name="Agent is registered in the VS-128 registry (W3931) with a proposed risk tier…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Agent is registered in the VS-128 registry (W3931) with a proposed risk tier; agent type, task scope, tool contracts, and owning team recorded — no AAP runtime identity is provisioned without this registry record
Responsible (R): AI-Governance Liaison
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: 1–2 hours/agent</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5512_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5512_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5512_Task12" name="Ethics/DPIA routing: any agent touching customers, employees, money, or…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Ethics/DPIA routing: any agent touching customers, employees, money, or personal data goes to the AI Ethics Review Board (W3952); an RA 10173 DPIA is opened where automated decisions affect data subjects (links to W3939)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / DPO
Accountable (A): AI Governance Lead
Duration: 1–2 hours/agent</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5512_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5512_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5512_Task13" name="Registered agent enters the evaluation pipeline (W5513); intake evidence —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Registered agent enters the evaluation pipeline (W5513); intake evidence — scorecards, SIB decision, registry record, DPIA disposition — archived for audit (links to W3949)
Responsible (R): AAP Platform Lead
Accountable (A): AAP Platform Lead
Duration: 0.5 hour/agent</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5512_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5512_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5512_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5512_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5512_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-616 (ensure controlled execution — AI Lifecycle Operations, Assurance &amp; Value Realization (PA-128.3).) | - operational: registration gate — no runtime identity without a VS-128 registry record | - operational: SIB use-EBS → build routing for every agent proposal
Owner: AAP Platform Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
